; stdlib-only — no libraries field, ever (AGENTS.md dependency firewall, I3).
;
; [node] holds the private-type definition + hash-consing + smart-constructor
;   normalization: a term's private record can only be built in its defining
;   module, so construction lives here and [Term]/[Context] expose the frozen
;   views. It is [private_modules] so no consumer can reach the raw builders
;   (I2: smart constructors via [Context] are the sole public construction path).
; [iarr_unsafe] holds the optional no-copy [Iarr] cast, private for the same
;   reason (ADR-0003 fixes B1).
; [atom_unsafe] holds the no-copy [int -> Atom.t] cast (same B1 pattern), private
;   so [Lit] can unpack a packed literal but no consumer can forge an atom id —
;   [Atom.fresh] is the only public minter (ADR-0005).

; [explanation] and [theory] are pure signatures (types + a module type, no
;   values) — the ADR-0005 THEORY vocabulary; they have no [.ml].

(library
 (name oxsmt_core)
 (private_modules node iarr_unsafe atom_unsafe)
 (modules_without_implementation explanation theory))
